Rules:
{"id": "RULE-001", "name": "Only current, savings and virtual accounts can be debited", "category": "validation", "statement": "A payment order can only be charged to an account of type CTE (current), AHO (savings) or VIR (virtual). Any other account type is rejected with error 50001 'TIPO DE CUENTA NO PERMITIDO'.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:33-39"]}
{"id": "RULE-002", "name": "Order must exist and be pending", "category": "validation", "statement": "The payment order, identified by order number and company, must exist and be in state 'P' (pending). If it is missing the error is 50002 'ORDEN NO EXISTE'; if it is in any other state the error is 50003 'ORDEN NO ESTA PENDIENTE'.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:41-59"]}
{"id": "RULE-003", "name": "Tariff lookup: company tariff first, else general service tariff", "category": "policy", "statement": "The commission tariff is the one agreed for the company and service. If the company has none, the general service tariff applies and the commission is never charged separately. A missing tariff counts as 0.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:61-77"]}
{"id": "RULE-004", "name": "Commission: web channel pays half, payroll pays none", "category": "calculation", "statement": "Orders from the WEB channel pay half of the tariff, rounded to 2 decimals. Every other channel pays the full tariff. The service 'NOMINA' (payroll) never pays commission.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:79-86"]}
{"id": "RULE-005", "name": "Total to debit includes commission unless charged separately", "category": "calculation", "statement": "The amount debited on the first movement is the order value plus the commission, unless the commission is charged separately (flag 'S'), in which case only the order value is debited.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:88-92"]}
{"id": "RULE-006", "name": "Sufficient funds check with overdraft allowance", "category": "validation", "statement": "Virtual accounts (VIR) cannot go below zero: the balance must cover the total to debit. Other accounts may overdraw up to 100.00. Otherwise the payment is rejected with error 50004 'FONDOS INSUFICIENTES'.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:94-106"]}
{"id": "RULE-007", "name": "Debit of the account and separate commission movement, all or nothing", "category": "lifecycle", "statement": "Inside one transaction the account is debited for the total with reference 'PAGO ORDEN', and its movement number is returned. If the commission is charged separately and is greater than zero, a second debit with reference 'COMISION PAGO' is made. A failure in either debit undoes the transaction and rejects the payment (50005 'ERROR EN DEBITO' or 50006 'ERROR EN COMISION').", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:108-141"]}
{"id": "RULE-008", "name": "Order marked as paid with processing date and commission", "category": "lifecycle", "statement": "After the debits, the order changes from pending to paid ('A'), recording the processing date as payment date and the commission charged. If the update fails or touches no row, everything is rolled back with error 50007 'ERROR ACTUALIZANDO ORDEN'. On success the message is 'PAGO REALIZADO'.", "sources": ["sp/sp_pago_orden.sp:143-164"]}
